  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of its excessive size, scale, design and height within the small amenity area of the site, would result in an overdevelopment of the site, causing harm to the existing dwelling and character of the wider area. It would therefore be contrary to D12.3 (Ensuring high quality design for all developments) and Policy D12.4 (Alterations and extensions to existing buildings).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, due to its size and proximity to the neighbouring properties, would be overbearing, visually intrusive and cause a loss of outlook to the amenity of the occupiers of No. 21 Montague Road and Ground Floor Flat at 23 Montague Road, contrary to Policy D12.3 (Ensuring high quality design for all developments) and Policy D12.4 (Alterations and extensions to existing buildings).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development, by reason of the internal space available to potential occupants and poor outlook, would result in a poor standard of accommodation and would be contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy D12.3 (Ensuring high quality design for all developments).",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of a legal agreement securing a carbon offset contribution, the application fails to demonstrate compliance with the Mayor's net-zero carbon target contrary to Merton Local Plan Policy CC2.2 (minimising greenhouse gas emissions).",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of a legal agreement securing a carbon offset contribution, the application fails to demonstrate compliance with the Mayor's net-zero carbon target contrary to Merton Local Plan Policy CC2.2 (minimising greenhouse gas emissions).",
    "Reason : 5 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\r\n\r\nThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\r\nIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
